New object literal created every render → new reference → React sees "changed" prop → re-render.

```jsx
// Bad: new ref each render
<Child config={{ theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' }} />

// Fix 1: useMemo
const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' }), []);
<Child config={config} />

// Fix 2: move outside component (if static)
const CONFIG = { theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' };
function Parent() {
  return <Child config={CONFIG} />;
}

// Fix 3: memo on Child
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => { ... });
```

JS equality: `{} !== {}`. Same content, different ref. React use `===` for prop compare.

Best fix depend on whether object value change over time:
- Static → outside component
- Derived from props/state → `useMemo`
- Can't change parent → `React.memo` on child
